{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342045-interesting-mixed-games","id":1342045,"title":"Interesting mixed games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-18T02:33:45-07:00","id":1342045,"title":"Interesting mixed games","content":"I'm curious - what, in everyone's opinion, would be the best/most fun/most workable combinations of only two splats for PCs to be run in a campaign?<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> <u>Prometheans and Sin-Eaters</u> - the Half-Alive and the Once-Dead. With a keen awareness of life's frailty, can the Bound aid in the Divine Fire's process of creating new souls? Will they agree to if they know what it may entail? And can the Created learn about humanity from those that have something close to aliens living in their heads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:15:46-07:00","id":1342162,"title":"","content":"I m having lot of fun as a gm in a beast+mage campaign.<br /> They seem to me like two faces of the same coin.<br /> Bright astral vs dark astral<br /> Broad but slow powers vs focused and fast powers<br /> Defend the weak vs prey on the weak.<br /> <br /> And creative players can find lot of combos to buff and help the two splats reciprocally, they seems to work very well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T17:41:14-07:00","id":1342232,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly fond of Ordo Dracul Vampires + Mages.<br /> They have quite a bit of overlap in goals and interests. As long as the Mysteries the the group is investigating don't stray from the material world or too far from civilization for too long vampires wouldn't have much problem.<br /> They also kind of cover each other's weaknesses. Mages get screwed by paradox when sleepers watch, vampires have tons of powers and tricks for controlling and manipulating mortals that can be used to make them go away. Vampires are harmed by fire and sunlight, a Mage with Forces can make those refuse to touch a vampire.<br /> <br /> Edit: It works especially well if the Vampires upon learning of the Mages fight against the Exarchs rule, then equate the Exarchs with the God that the Ordo Dracul is determined to fight. It's not that God became senile or whatever. The heavens are being run by a bunch of idiotic usurpers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-18-2019, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T17:51:16-07:00","id":1342234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342045-interesting-mixed-games?p=1342162#post1342162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defend the weak vs prey on the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>*snorts into his chicken soup* Yeah, sure.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I might have an easier time trying to think of a pairing I wouldn't have fun with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:01:49-07:00","id":1342421,"title":"","content":"The Arisen and the Damed, Vampires are running a Mummies cult and the neonates get to serve with the mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T00:39:19-07:00","id":1342487,"title":"","content":"I know it isn't out yet, but I fully intend to integrate Deviant into my Changeling Chronicle. Two types of individuals, both of whom were changed from human into something else. Both trying to figure out what to do now that they aren't who they used to be. Imagine you are taken, only to come home and find out that something took your place. Only, that something was taken too - it was used as fuel to process an experiment to change someone else, and now part of you - the part of you that the keeper used to make this fetch - is woven into this strangers soul. This stranger who wasn't taken by the Gentry, but by people - people who somehow knew your other half wasn't what it appeared to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:34:13-07:00","id":1343068,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna cheat here and pick three, so sorry.<br /> <br /> I've been really wanting to run and/or play a Beast/Sin-Eater/Werewolf game; all three are essentially the Boundary people's of the otherworldly realms (Astral, Underworld, Shadow), and running a game with all three and exploring the idea of belonging to two worlds would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T03:29:43-07:00","id":1343740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342045-interesting-mixed-games?p=1343068#post1343068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna cheat here and pick three, so sorry.<br /> <br /> I've been really wanting to run and/or play a Beast/Sin-Eater/Werewolf game; all three are essentially the Boundary people's of the otherworldly realms (Astral, Underworld, Shadow), and running a game with all three and exploring the idea of belonging to two worlds would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs up\ud83d\udc4d\ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T10:32:37-07:00","id":1344014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342045-interesting-mixed-games?p=1343068#post1343068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna cheat here and pick three, so sorry.<br /> <br /> I've been really wanting to run and/or play a Beast/Sin-Eater/Werewolf game; all three are essentially the Boundary people's of the otherworldly realms (Astral, Underworld, Shadow), and running a game with all three and exploring the idea of belonging to two worlds would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we're gonna cheat, the game I have always wanted to run has been a Forsaken, Lost, Sin-Eater, Descent, and Primordial crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T10:41:25-07:00","id":1344017,"title":"","content":"I Think that I would have to go with the Fallen and the Arisen. I would like to think that i would dig the subtle political stories, with the occasional pants-shitting terror that both splats bring to the table. and if i could, i would definitely through in some beasts. they create strategic uncertainty really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T17:10:08-07:00","id":1344097,"title":"","content":"Well the first one is selfish, as its the game-idea I've wanted to do for years but, haven't really gotten to properly start yet. This is the idea I'd personally want to use my primary character for, the Scarlet Witch (whom I named without realizing was an X-men character &gt;.&gt; embarrassing embarrassing.) The story arc I wanted to do, was Scarlet is obsessed with werewolf history and integrates with a pack that slowly become interested in her investigations into Father Wolf... Integrating material from The Sundered World, this Mage/Werewolf crossover idea sounds perfect for exploring stuff like, what did the Exarchs have to do with, if anything, the fall of Urfarah? And explore the Forsaken/Pure divide with modern Forsaken witnessing the ancient world.<br /> <br /> Plus, with Mages, even without all that nonsense I just mentioned that are my peeersonal obsessions? Well, Mages just grant wider access to creatures Werewolves might want to, or *need* to Hunt, for possibly many different reasons. How about a Werewolf pack whose territory sprouted an Abyssal Verge? Just taking the gulmoths and aberrations and forgetting any Mage characters, I think the Uratha would have an interesting time with such terrors!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But if I were to give an answer that's probably more interesting to a wider group, I can't see how Vampire/Demon isn't just *perfect*. Conspiracies involving VII, the God-Machine's influence on Vlad Tepes, The God-Machine sabotaging or subsuming Lancea et Sanctum, Temptors and Daevas having nights out on the town and making deals, Ordo Dracul working with gadget-smiths to heighten their mutual crafts, not to mention both sides are mistrusting and paranoid so the LACK of cooperation would just BREED drama... The strix mess with Infrastructure, demons might want to weaponize that, aggravating or intriguing the local Prince. How about a cult that's half Circle of the Crone, half Demon? They're just a good combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T21:28:05-07:00","id":1344122,"title":"","content":"I'll be perfectly honest: I really wanna see how a Vampire/Deviant chronicle focused on all the weird mutant one-offs that orbit Divergence and the Curse looks, because those two games are inarguably the closest standard characters get to cosmology-blind outside of Hunter and that opens the door for all sorts of out-of-context weirdness even without leaning into the shared lens of body horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:17:40-07:00","id":1344690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342045-interesting-mixed-games?p=1342162#post1342162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m having lot of fun as a gm in a beast+mage campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the topic of Beast+Mage, Dave's post in the Mage forums reminded me of a delightfully terrible concept I had when I was brainstorming how (or if) to use Beasts in my mage chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1344632#post1344632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there's the Harrowed, who suffered a metamorphic Awakening in which the part of the Watchtower's process that replaces Integrity with Wisdom failed. Being a mage who still has an Integrity rating sucks on a &quot;living nightmare&quot; level; their own powers cause breaking points, and their Mage Sight, including the Peripheral sense for anything supernatural or understanding High Speech, is actively painful. They don't tend to live very long.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Best</b> Lair ever.<br /> <br /> <br /> More on topic, though: my favorite crossover combination has always been Geist+Changeling, although I haven't had a chance to play or run such a game. They work really well together for themes of defining community, healing, and self-realization. It makes a great combination for exploring very mundane human-centric themes with a supernatural twist. That's not necessarily in my list of favorite genres, but I would like to play in that kind of game at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 10-30-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T11:39:45-07:00","id":1344704,"title":"","content":"So, any community that has hosted a Harrowed within the last few years is positively riddled with potential Chambers in random places, many with a lower public profile than the site of some old torture dungeon or abandoned prison. Nice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T18:54:01-07:00","id":1344798,"title":"","content":"One of the best games I've been in involved a mummy, a werewolf, a mage, a slasher, and a hunter traveling to the Underworld. The werewolf eventually died off and the player made a demon, which was actually the first time we had a chance to do anything with that particular system.<br /> <br /> In terms of good synergy, a Vampire/Mummy crossover would be fun, especially in Mummy 2E, where your vampire friend's power fluctuates in a really weird way each time you wake up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:50:50-08:00","id":1347317,"title":"","content":"There's definitely a few I'd love to run or play in, but there's one I keep coming back to in particular:<br /> <br /> See, <i>years</i> ago, maybe back on the old forum even, someone at some point floated the idea of Mummy + Promethean, and something about that just seemed to click. Themes of growth and discovery clashing with themes of age and glories long past, the growing fires of Azoth and the ebbing light of Sekhem, Disquiet and Sybaris tangling together in weird and horrifying ways... and yet there's potential for a parent-adopted child(ren) bond with the right players, and unique stepping stones on the Pilgrimage through that weird lens. Even the Arisen's Descent ending could prove an interesting metaphor for the loss of a parent, and every interaction with the cult could be a weird metaphorical glimpse at extended family.<br /> <br /> Ideally, it'd be a smaller group; my current mental image for it is perhaps one Arisen and (at least initially) one Created, the former stirred to awakening after a (possibly now-dead, possibly not, possibly doomed) cultist went Progenitor to create the latter. The cult freaks out, wakes up their god for input, chronicle ensues. Maybe they encounter and &quot;adopt&quot; another one or two Prometheans in the process, and the family grows. Or maybe they don't, and it's one &quot;parent&quot; and one &quot;child&quot; alone against a very, very weird world. Maybe another Mummy or two come in, but... admittedly, not how I'm currently picturing it.<br /> <br /> Now, you'd have to figure out how to juggle how Disquiet affects or doesn't affect the Arisen or their cult for the purposes of the story and potentially the same with Sybaris depending on how it works in 2e. Could always handwave them for the themes, and to avoid some... potentially uncomfortable implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-09-2019, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:13:59-08:00","id":1347939,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think there's a 'best', and it depends really on what you're going for. Epic battles on a god-tier scale and conceptual shenanigans? Demon and Mage with xp galore would be my advice.<br /> If you want to do a real War Dogs story, about a tightly-knit group with supremely strong bonds stuck in a shitty situation, I think Beast/Werewolf offers great synergy (put the focus on the Pack/Family Bonds, explore how they hold up, or assume they're basically anime-style best friends forever and use horrible, horrible circumstances to make them appreciate this light in a dark world).<br /> Promethean would work really well with Geist, if you're going for the introspective route and want to explore human nature and e.g. the concept of consequences on society (How do you stop people from robbing if that is the only way for them to feed their family in this town? Figure that out, make Promethean happy in the process, satisfy Bound/Geist by solving the problem and thus achieve some semblance of 'justice' - resolve anchorage). Will be a comparatively short-lived cooperation due to disquiet, so likely a bittersweet chronicle.<br /> Geist and Changeling could also work great, as would Changeling and Beast, if you're up for a &quot;explore a fantastically horrifying world&quot; type of deal.<br /> Lots of Intrigue? Demon/Mummy (and/or Vampire). Vampire/Mummy especially lends itself to long-running, time setting-skipping chronicles and power plays.<br /> Generally, you can stick Beast anywhere, and it'll work (albeit there might be better options, again depending on your goals). I think Beast/Mage would be a lot of fun (especially with Whispers or Beasts bent on exploring Chambers joining a Mage Cabal that is Mystery Search Inc.), as would be Geist/Beast (here, a revenge-driven plot would likely be easiest to achieve).<br /> <br /> My 2 cents for now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}